# Machine-written round evidence — reformatting a 250KB trace is churn, and
# every archived round failed the gate until this line existed.
rounds/*.json
# A crashed run is the same artifact by another name: the driver writes it when a
# round dies part-way, and it lands in the repo the moment anyone commits with
# `git add -A`. Missing here cost a red CI on 2026-08-23 — round 203's browser
# died, the dump was archived, and `prettier --check .` refused it.
crashes/*.json
# The same artifact a third time: rounds recovered from those crash records by
# `scripts/salvage-crashed.mjs`. Machine-written round evidence like the two
# above, and it failed this gate on the very run that created it.
rounds-salvaged/*.json
